.TH ES32-TOP 1 "September 2026" "es32-top 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
es32-top \- Rust ESP32 runtime manager and terminal monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B es32-top
.I COMMAND
[.I OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B es32-top
manages versioned ESP32 workloads and provides a dependency-free terminal
monitor over USB serial. The host implementation is Rust; the ESP32 runtime
is Arduino/ESP-IDF compatible C++.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tui --port PATH
Render live CPU, memory, network, flash, PSRAM, and task telemetry.
.TP
.B workload list|inspect|install|start|stop|restart|remove|logs|quarantine
Manage the persistent workload registry.
.TP
.B package build|verify
Build or verify a native directory .espkg package with SHA-256 payload hashes.
.TP
.B storage analyze
Explain flash pressure and potentially recoverable storage.
.TP
.B doctor
Report failed or quarantined workloads.
.TP
.B support-bundle -o DIRECTORY
Export device metadata, workload records, and audit history.
.TP
.B simulate
Emit a protocol workload-list frame without hardware.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --registry FILE
Use an alternate local registry. Default is ~/.config/es32-top/workloads.json.
.TP
.B --list-ports
List candidate serial devices.
.SH FILES
.I esp/esp.ino
Legacy telemetry firmware.
.br
.I runtime/esp_runtime/esp_runtime.ino
ESP-Top runtime scaffold.